<title>HONG KONG: South China Ind 1996 net down 73 pct.</title>
<headline>South China Ind 1996 net down 73 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   12.0	 vs 46.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0	  vs 4.5</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	21.36 gain vs 149.23 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    65.30	vs 244.65</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,427.69   vs 1,605.91</p>
<p>    Company name		 South China Industries Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 4-6</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 23</p>
<p>NOTE - South China Industries is a maker of toys, hair care products and shoes.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of interest in South China Strategic Ltd of approximately HK$17.47 million and write-back of loss on restructuring of a subsidiary in 1995 of approximately HK$3.89 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs 15 cents (including interim dividend and speical bonus).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
